  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved decent work employment opportunities through the development of coherent policies and programmes aligned to international standards on labour statistics in Tuvalu</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In October 2017, the International Labour Organization (ILO) and the Pacific Community (SPC) signed a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) to enhance labour market information systems and statistics in the Pacific, supporting the monitoring of Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs). The MoU focuses on improving data analysis, collection, and the capacity of Pacific Island Countries to conduct relevant surveys. It also promotes sharing of labour-related microdata and enhances capacity development in data production. Collaborating with the SPC&apos;s Statistics for Development Division, the ILO developed labour force modules for surveys, approved in 2019, benefiting various stakeholders and promoting decent work opportunities in Tuvalu. ILO has since added modules such as the recent ILO-SPC Climate Change module in 2025. The beneficiaries in this area of work are the bureau of statistics, government agencies, donors and the Tuvalu tripartite and development partners, training institutions and the citizens of Tuvalu. The Labour Force Survey training is jointly conducted by ILO, SPC and the Bureau of statistics and the Tuvalu tripartite partners, Government agencies, academic and training institutions and the development partners.</narrative>
  </description>
